# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# .gitignore for Go modules
# Best-practices: ignore build artifacts, editor/IDE files, OS temp files, and
# local secrets. Keep module files like go.mod and go.sum in source control.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Binaries for programs and plugins
*.exe
*.dll
*.so
*.dylib

# Test binary and common build outputs
*.test
*.out
coverage.out
*.coverprofile

# If you build to a `bin/` directory, ignore it
/bin/

# Output of the go tool when using -i or when building packages
*.o
*.a

# Dependency directories
# If you vendor dependencies and commit them, remove this line.
vendor/

# Go workspace file (optional)
# If you use a committed go.work for multi-module workspaces, remove this line.
go.work

# Editor/IDE directories and files
.idea/
.vscode/
*.iml

# macOS
.DS_Store

# Windows
Thumbs.db

# Linux/temporary swap and editor backup files
*~
# vim swap files
.swp

# Environment files that may contain secrets
.env
*.env

# Logs
*.log

# Misc
# Keep these generic, but avoid ignoring files you intentionally track
.cache/

# Per-module and temporary build directories
**/bin/
**/tmp/

# Local configuration (uncommitted user settings)
.local-config

# End of file

learnGoWithTests/maps/v2/go.mod